WEBVTT

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:38.640
Hey.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:44.820
You're not gonna get mad at me for entering without knocking?

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.040
I see you're still out of it.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.390
I'm fine. My neck's just a little sore.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.790
Did you take your pain medication?

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:55.710
Medication?

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:59.170
How do you forget something you take every day?

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.230
Hurry up and take it, idiot.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:25.820
You aren't trying to find your key, are you?

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.070
Yeah.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.470
I have it.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.440
You forgot again?

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.170
Does it hurt?

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:49.890
No.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.680
If you fall, I'll carry you to bed,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.520
so feel free to do your rehab stuff while I'm here.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.870
Okay.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.300
Then make some tea.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.080
What would you like?

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.010
What? Melon soda.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.060
Didn't you say tea?

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.950
What are you saying? I don't like bitter things.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.580
That's right.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.840
You can tell me if there's something wrong.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.410
If you're not feeling well, we can go back to the hospital.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.530
<i>You can't go to the hospital!</i>

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:27.830
What?

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.320
I'm fine. I don't need to go to the hospital.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.060
<i>As I recall,</i>

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.660
<i>we all went to the mountain villa.</i>

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.820
<i>But what happened after that?</i>

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.340
<i>We went to see the meteor shower at Shinano.</i>

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:50.950
<i>And then...</i>

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.950
I killed...

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.330
I killed a man.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.410
<i>And then, I...</i>

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.710
<i>fell from the cliff.</i>

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.550
Hey.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.070
You're spilling it.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.330
You haven't eaten anything since this morning, right?

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:18.770
You should really eat something.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:19.770
Yeah.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.400
Thank you.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:29.610
I have to go now, but go to sleep early tonight.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.000
I'll come again tomorrow.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.110
Why do you look so surprised?

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.170
Forget it. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.440
<i>Am I confused again?</i>

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.360
<i>I lost my memories and met Orion...</i>

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.010
<i>I thought I was finally remembering things again, but...</i>

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:17.870
<i>Was that... a dream?</i>

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.120
<i>Why...</i>

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.990
<i>did Shin do that?</i>

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.380
<i>Could this be a dream?</i>

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.010
<i>No, the biting coldness of the water feels too real.</i>

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:38.530
This is reality.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.660
You were sleeping?

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.510
Good morning.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.690
Today's our one-year anniversary.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.830
You're okay with not doing anything?

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:15.760
Well, I suppose we should do something...

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.110
You forgot, didn't you?

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.370
Yeah.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:22.560
Thought so.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:24.210
Sorry.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:25.810
Actually,

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:29.620
it's only been three months since we started dating.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:34.370
You've been doing your best to match your story with mine since yesterday,

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.980
but you can't fool me anymore.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:38.920
Your memories

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.290
are all messed up, aren't they?

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:44.540
<i>He figured it out.</i>

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.410
When I kissed you in the hospital yesterday,

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.820
you didn't get embarrassed and flip out like you normally would've.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.550
And our conversations don't really mesh.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:54.830
What's going on?

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:03.560
I didn't know how or what to explain.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:10.320
And I didn't want to go back to the hospital, so...

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.320
I understand.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.110
I promise I won't take you back to the hospital.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:16.090
Really?

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:18.270
So you don't need to hide anything anymore.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:21.460
It'd be stranger if you thought you could hide it.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:26.460
You may have lost your memories, but you're still the same idiot, idiot.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.550
Let's go out.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:31.890
Where to?

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.250
Just come.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:39.910
You haven't said my name since yesterday.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:41.970
You've forgotten it, haven't you?

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.480
Then I'll explain from the start.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.660
My name is Shin.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.400
We're old friends.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.490
And like I said before,

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.280
we've been dating for three months.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:58.490
<i>So I've been dating Shin.</i>

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:02.740
You really don't remember anything, do you?

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.000
I hope this'll help you get your memories back.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.250
This is the college you're attending.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.380
I may be your junior, but I'm a senior at the adjacent high school.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.500
The college and high school share a campus.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:27.590
The thing that's most likely to still be in your memories is your club activities.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.270
You've been in a band since your second year of high school.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:31.940
As a vocalist.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.360
I... sing?

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.830
You were really terrible when you started,

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.560
but you were okay by your third year.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:41.280
I haven't heard many of your songs since you started college,

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.150
but you were always enthusiastic about them.

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:48.750
This is the clubroom.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:50.250
Look familiar?

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:57.290
Before your accident, you were practicing twice a week.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:01.060
I came here often after classes.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:06.140
I enjoyed watching you really get into it.

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:10.650
We talked a lot here afterward.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.920
The first time I told you how I felt

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:21.950
and the first time I kissed you

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.400
both happened here.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:29.350
Since then, I've kissed you countless times, but...

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.230
You can't remember?

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:02.450
I'm sorry. I won't do it anymore.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:07.960
I thought if I kissed you here, you might remember something, but...

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:13.310
Right now, I'm a stranger to you.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:15.950
I'm sorry.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.500
If you apologize like that to me,

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:19.810
it'll just...

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:25.950
By the way...

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:30.970
You're supposed to go back to work starting tomorrow.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:32.910
<i>Work?</i>

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.920
<i>Does he mean... that café?</i>

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.220
Here?

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.070
Hey, where are you going?

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.340
Side entrance.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.000
Idiot. Where do you think you are?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.160
This isn't where you work.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:56.840
<i>Toma?</i>

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.510
Are you all right?

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.030
He said your memories are all messed up.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.270
This is Toma.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:20.590
I thought it would be troubling if there was no one you could rely on at work,

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:21.900
so I told him.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.480
So? How much have you forgotten?

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.710
Have you completely forgotten me?

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:29.900
She seems to have forgotten almost everything.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:34.560
What do you mean, "seems"? You should explain everything to her.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:37.670
She should find out what she can for herself.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.490
Here we go again.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:44.130
You've probably forgotten that this guy has been like this since he was a kid.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.880
And you've always been too soft.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.900
<i>It seems like they haven't changed.</i>

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:51.650
In any case, Toma, I need you to help her out at work.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:54.800
Of course. I was planning on it from the start.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:58.750
When my cheeky younger brother asks me to look after my adorable sister,

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.110
how could I possibly say no?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.080
Thank you.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:06.410
So are you really starting tomorrow?

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:10.580
Yeah. I guess that's the plan.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.680
Wanting to keep her memory troubles a secret is fine,

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.930
but you <i>did</i> take her to the hospital, right?

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:16.500
Yeah.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:21.120
Shouldn't she take some time off from work?

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:21.870
If something happened...

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.250
There's no guarantee she'll get better if she rests.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:29.010
Oh, you work at a place called "Maid's Sheep."

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.550
You don't even remember the accident?

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.660
Or why the accident happened...

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:42.930
I sort of remember.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:45.760
Like why you fell?

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:48.200
I think I slipped.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:49.720
I see.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:55.470
<i>Was Shin there with me when the accident happened?</i>

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:04.020
<i>That memory might've been a dream.</i>

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:04.750
Hey...

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:11.710
What?

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:14.800
Nothing. Never mind.

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:20.060
<i>What?</i>

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.840
<i>What was he about to say?</i>

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.740
You oversleep too much.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.990
Try to maintain a schedule.

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:46.310
I'm sorry.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:48.480
If you have time to apologize, get moving.

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:52.730
Well, here it is.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:53.450
What about you?

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:57.240
Huh? Oh, I have prep school now.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.710
I'll come pick you up when you get off work.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:00.630
Are you sure?

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.580
You don't need to worry about that.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:03.410
Thank you.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:08.420
Oh, right. Do you remember it?

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.480
"It"?

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:12.640
I told you yesterday, the greeting.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.060
You don't say "Welcome,"

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.720
but "Welcome back, master."

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:19.580
Yeah.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.330
And when you see customers off?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.440
This isn't the time to be embarrassed, idiot.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:33.320
T-Take care, master.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:42.360
Looks like you'll be okay.

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:48.700
Well, hello.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:49.960
It's been a while.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:55.350
<i>Huh? Waka seems a little different.</i>

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:56.380
What's wrong?

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.680
You look dazed.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.640
You're not back to full health yet?

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.030
I'm all right.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.390
Don't push yourself.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:09.130
Still, a bandaged maid would bring in customers just by being here!

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:14.900
But I'm glad you didn't get any scratches on that adorable face of yours!

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:19.060
If you did, this café's reputation would be...

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:22.230
Oh dear, just thinking about it gives me the willies!

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:26.440
Are you <i>really</i> worried about her?

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:29.440
Good morning, Mine! You're looking cute again today!

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.460
Don't try to fool me.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:33.940
So, you're back in today?

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.920
Good morning!

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:42.180
I promised I'd help out, but you got here first.

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:48.050
Mr. Manager, she hasn't worked in a while, so go easy on her.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:53.650
Oh Toma, I was just giving her words of encouragement.

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.460
Good morning!

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.650
Oh, Sawa. Morning.

00:15:57.650 --> 00:15:58.560
Hey!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.740
It's been a little while!

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:02.530
Are you okay?

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.910
Yeah. I'm sorry I worried you.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:09.220
You've really had it rough.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:11.460
But you're looking better than I expected, so I'm glad.

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:14.840
I didn't know what would happen to you after the accident.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:17.260
Yeah, I was really surprised.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:21.650
<i>So Sawa and Mine were both with me at the time.</i>

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.000
I fell from the cliff, right?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.420
Huh? Didn't Shin tell you anything?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.910
Not really.

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:36.650
Okay. Then I'll tell you everything I know about that day.

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:37.280
Okay.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:43.030
Shin, Toma, Waka, Mine, you, and I went on a trip to Shinano, right?

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:45.380
Yeah.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:49.960
It was an orientation trip for work, right?

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:51.340
That's right.

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:52.660
The members...

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:54.960
The people who work here part-time.

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:57.790
Then what about Ikki and Kento?

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:03.060
Oh, those two joined us by chance at the mountain retreat.

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:05.420
Did you know them?

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:09.220
C'mon, get it together.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.230
<i>Our stories don't seem to match...</i>

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:20.060
<i>I'm confused about what happened on the trip.</i>

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:25.280
<i>Was it a long dream I had while I was in the hospital?</i>

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:31.960
When it got dark, Shin, who was supposed to have gone out with you, came back all pale,

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:36.860
and said you fell from a cliff and he didn't know where you were.

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:41.130
After we heard that, we all panicked.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.510
You were all at the villa?

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:47.370
Didn't we all go out to see the meteor shower?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.690
What are you talking about?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:54.150
So, everyone at the mountain villa went on a giant search.

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:57.850
That's when Ikki, Kento, and someone else...

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.530
I can't remember his name,

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.400
but I think he said he was a photographer?

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:06.510
He helped us look, too.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.400
Then after we all looked for about an hour,

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.170
we finally found you collapsed at the bottom of the cliff.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:15.690
So that's what happened.

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:21.680
But when we found you, Shin was seriously creeping me out.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.730
What do you mean?

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:29.180
I'm not sure how to answer that, but he was weirdly calm or...

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:35.360
This was in contrast with Toma, who was running around in a panic.

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:40.870
<i>The Shinano trip was real, but...</i>

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:45.370
<i>The part about seeing the meteor shower was different.</i>

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:47.950
<i>What about the cause of my injury?</i>

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.720
<i>Maybe I'll check with Shin.</i>

00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:00.040
<i>This person...</i>

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:01.250
Um...

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:06.090
To think that you'd talk to me...

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:09.140
It makes me happy.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.010
Long time no see.

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:15.770
Huh? Is this our first meeting?

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:19.480
No, I'm pretty sure we met at the mountain villa this time.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:21.770
Are your injuries all right?

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:25.650
From the accident...

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:31.160
Hey! What are you doing?

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:35.570
When I went to pick you up, they said you already left!

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.540
Don't go off by yourself.

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.490
What if something happened?

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:42.140
Yeah.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:50.160
It's cool for August, isn't it?

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:54.220
The weatherman seemed pretty worried about the abnormal weather.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:58.870
I wonder if it'll stay like this until autumn.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:01.060
With the way it feels, that might be the case.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.810
Do you remember that first performance?

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.840
Performance? Mine?

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:12.570
Yeah.

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.140
No.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:15.780
I see.

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:19.330
After the performance, I said terrible things to you.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.790
Like, "What kind of performance was that?"

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:24.450
"Do you even want people to hear it?"

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:29.590
"Your voice was barely audible, and it wasn't something you could listen to."

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:32.360
I was really preaching.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.970
And I made you cry.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:39.980
So you don't remember.

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:43.630
I still say some mean things sometimes,

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:50.450
but now that I think about it, having no memories is far more difficult than I had thought.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:56.900
Um... Can I ask you about the accident?

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:58.000
What?

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:02.750
What happened that night on the Shinano trip?

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:06.960
I'm sorry.

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:10.830
It was my fault.

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:16.080
I hurt you.

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:18.150
What do you mean?

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.580
About the accident...

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:24.650
Sorry. I haven't sorted out my feelings about it yet.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:27.360
Um...

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:30.400
I don't have the confidence to tell you about it calmly.

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:34.220
In any case, it was my fault.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.870
That's all I can say right now.

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:41.370
I'm sorry. Forgive me.

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.930
<i>Did I make him angry?</i>

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:48.990
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:51.470
Can — hear —?

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:56.010
My voice... Hey, you...

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:29.500
Wow, you were the vocalist for a band!

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:31.280
I'd like to try that, too.

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:33.200
Huh? What part would I play?

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:35.660
Lead guitar and vocals, of course!

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:39.220
And I'd headbang death-metal style, like this...

00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:40.470
You don't understand?
